      "evidence": "The Statement declares “δ_1,…,δ_n” but assumes “|δ_i|≤u for every i<n” and forms “∏_{i<n}(1+δ_i).” The library’s indexing convention is zero-based (for example, the dot-product theorem uses x_0,…,x_{n-1}); at n=1 this product requires δ_0, which was never declared. Under one-based reading it instead omits δ_n. Thus the quantified product is not defined as written.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "6214b8b1e689a91b06adcf217ad3cd3b9cccfb1b4f21cad7951d41080ce2daff"
    },
    {
