      "location": "Proof step 2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 2.1 says, “A matrix B satisfies ||A-B||_2≤τ with rank k exactly when k satisfies σ_{k+1}≤τ.” Step 1.1 only gives the minimum distance among matrices of rank at most k, hence licenses existence of a suitable B, not this assertion for every rank-k B. Take A=diag(1,0), τ=0, k=1, and B=2diag(1,0). Here σ_2=0≤τ and rank B=1, but ||A-B||_2=1>0.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "6373044453624d7b87d49bdb6dd5c5057c90f613a1325fda7f219ae89232db25"
